# Employer Architecture Rules

## What the Employer Side IS

A talent discovery platform. Employers find verified candidates and make first contact. Period.

## What the Employer Side IS NOT

- NOT an ATS (no interview scheduling, no offer letters, no onboarding workflows)
- NOT an HRIS (no payroll, benefits, compliance tracking)
- NOT a background check company (MVR ordering is the ONLY exception)
- NOT a reporting/analytics platform (V1 has zero analytics)

If a feature belongs after the employer decides to hire someone, it does NOT belong in this app.

## Banned Patterns

### Do NOT add pipeline complexity

The candidate pipeline has exactly **3 statuses**:

| Status | DB value | Meaning |
|--------|----------|---------|
| New | `submitted` | Just applied or saved from talent search |
| Contacted | `contacted` | Employer has reached out |
| Archived | `archived` | Not interested / passed / already hired elsewhere |

**NEVER** add statuses like "Reviewing", "Interviewing", "Offer Sent", "Hired", or "Rejected". Those are ATS features. We are not an ATS.

```typescript
// ✅ ALLOWED — the only 3 pipeline columns
const PIPELINE_COLUMNS = [
  { status: 'submitted',  label: 'New',       color: 'blue'  },
  { status: 'contacted',  label: 'Contacted',  color: 'teal'  },
  { status: 'archived',   label: 'Archived',   color: 'gray'  },
]

// ❌ BANNED — ATS territory
{ status: 'interview',   label: 'Interviewing' }
{ status: 'offer',       label: 'Offer Sent'   }
{ status: 'hired',       label: 'Hired'        }
{ status: 'under_review', label: 'Reviewing'   }
```

### Do NOT create career-specific search pages

There is ONE talent search page: `TalentSearchPage.tsx`. It uses block-type filters that work across ALL career categories.

```typescript
// ❌ BANNED — career-specific discovery pages
'find-drivers'     // REMOVED — do not recreate
'find-developers'  // do not create
'find-nurses'      // do not create

// ✅ CORRECT — one search with dynamic filters
'talent-search'    // filters adapt to block registry categories
```

Block-type filters in Talent Search must be **derived from the block registry**, not hardcoded to specific careers. When a new career category is added (nursing, logistics, etc.), talent search filters should appear automatically.

### Do NOT build employer-side reports or analytics (V1)

The `reports` route and `ReportsPage.tsx` are being removed. Do not recreate them or add analytics dashboards, compliance reports, or hiring metrics.

If analytics are added post-launch, they must be limited to: views per job, contacts made, time-to-first-contact. Nothing more.

### Do NOT duplicate candidate data management

Employers read candidate data through career cards. They do NOT manage candidate data.

```typescript
// ✅ ALLOWED — read-only views of candidate data
GET /api/employer/talent/[userId]          // view career card
GET /api/employer/talent/[userId]/dot-app  // view DOT app

// ✅ ALLOWED — employer's own private data about candidates
POST /api/employer/candidate-data          // employer's private notes

// ❌ BANNED — employers editing candidate data
PUT /api/employer/talent/[userId]/profile  // never
PATCH /api/candidate/...                   // from employer context, never
```

## EmployerShell Routing

These are the ONLY routes EmployerShell should handle:

| Route | Component | Purpose |
|-------|-----------|---------|
| `null` (default) | `EmployerHub` | Main dashboard |
| `company-setup` | `CompanyOnboarding` | First-time company setup (blocking) |
| `company-profile` | `CompanyOnboarding` | Edit company profile |
| `talent-search` | `TalentSearchPage` | Single discovery page for ALL career categories |
| `post-job` | `JobPostingForm` | Create/edit job posting |
| `applicants` | `ApplicantsPage` | Full-page view of candidate pool |
| `team` | `TeamManagement` | Manage team members |
| `messages` | `MessageInbox` | Direct messaging |
| `stormchain` | `StormChainView` | STORM token info |

Any route not in this table requires explicit approval before adding.

